# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v19
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v18, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run49_participant_package_v18_checksums.sha256 and is pinned to the commit whose
# blobs it describes, ad4f614. This record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# RUN 51, THE DELIVERY OF WHAT RUN 50 STOPPED ON. TWENTY-THREE of the seventy files moved, and
# ALL SIX SEQUENCE-BEARING FILES ARE AMONG THEM. That is stated first because it is what a
# reader most needs to know, and every one of the six carries its OWN named exception record
# below and in server/tools/participant_packages.py, rather than being excused by widening a
# comparison. Their authority is the owner's rulings 1 to 6 of 2026-08-22 (Run 51 order,
# section 3).
#
# THE SIX SEQUENCE-BEARING EXCEPTIONS, EACH NAMED, EACH WITH WHAT MOVED INSIDE IT:
#
# assets/js/deepdive.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Rulings 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6. (a) The Portfolio Health
#   flyout is DELETED: renderCat8Health, CAT8_MODULES, cat8HealthData, cat8HealthDataFromLive,
#   isSnapshotStale and cat8Retired, together with the three buttons inside it. It rendered
#   nowhere and had no caller anywhere in the served application; an unreachable button is not
#   a control, and grep across assets, index.html and research returns no reference to it.
#   (b) The eight-module compliance panel is SPLIT into two panels, one per current category.
#   (c) The two maps that held the panel LABEL and the panel BUCKET are replaced by ONE table of
#   category KEYS, from which the label and the bucket are BOTH derived through the loaded
#   taxonomy, so they can no longer disagree; seven mis-filings are corrected by it.
#   (d) The grouping loop's bound is derived from the taxonomy instead of the literal ten, so
#   the eleventh project-level category can render at all. (e) En dashes and an ampersand in
#   rendered prose are replaced by words. NO STEP OF THE DECISION SEQUENCE, no reveal gate, no
#   lock, no randomization, no server contract and no append-only record moved.
#
# assets/js/decision.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Ruling 2. The action-plan trigger lines stopped
#   concatenating a category identifier and a module identifier into rendered text; they now
#   name the category and the module. The field they read is renamed from `num` to `key`, which
#   is what it is. No rule, no severity, no threshold and no ordering moved.
#
# assets/js/decision-ui.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Ruling 4. Rendered placeholders that were a
#   bare em dash now say "not recorded". The three inert "period: 1" literals are untouched.
#
# assets/js/workspace.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Ruling 4. The same placeholder correction, at the
#   date formatter the Run 51 order names explicitly and at five rendered status and provenance
#   fields. No control, no stage, no lock and no ordering moved.
#
# assets/questionnaires/intake.json -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Ruling 4. Em dashes in participant-
#   facing labels are replaced by words: each credential label reads "Project Management
#   Professional (PMP)" rather than "PMP - Project Management Professional", and the three
#   placeholder notices read as sentences. NO ITEM, NO RESPONSE OPTION, NO SCALE AND NO ORDER
#   CHANGED: the change is wording inside existing labels and notes.
#
# assets/questionnaires/debrief.json -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. Ruling 4. One em dash in the
#   placeholder notice. No item, no response option, no scale and no order changed.
#
# THE SEVENTEEN OTHERS, NONE SEQUENCE-BEARING:
#
# assets/js/app.js -- rulings 2 and section 6.1. The Signal Ledger's module and category
#   identifier chips are removed; the About page's counts are filled from the taxonomy.
# assets/js/knowledge.js -- section 6.1 and ruling 4. The handbook's "96 registered modules"
#   and every other typed count now derive; the Signal Stack SVG's ten identifier labels and
#   its accessible name are corrected.
# assets/js/taxonomy.js, assets/js/categories.js -- GENERATED. Regenerated from
#   build_client_taxonomy.py after the authority's `num` field became `key` and after the
#   generator began emitting window.LIN_TAXONOMY_COUNTS.
# assets/js/detail.js, assets/js/signals.js, assets/js/neural_flow.js,
#   assets/js/projectnet2d.js, assets/js/export.js -- ruling 2, the key/label separation, plus
#   the placeholder and dash corrections.
# assets/js/ds_defensibility_data.js, assets/js/charts3d.js, assets/js/auditor.js,
#   assets/js/admin-ops.js, assets/js/ingest.js, assets/js/store.js,
#   assets/visualizations/pceif_neural_signal_flow.html -- ruling 4 only.
# index.html -- section 6.1. Three typed counts become spans filled from the taxonomy.
#
# NO SERVER COMPUTATION MOVED: 101 registered, 63 in service, voting exactly A1.7 and A1.8, no
# stored figure changed, and the behaviour digest is unchanged. The v18 record is NOT
# regenerated: it is pinned to the commit whose blobs it describes.
#
